        "comments": "The assembly daEupNemo5.hap1.1 is based on 30x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 5 (20.72 Mbp - 22.86 Mbp), chromosome 6 (18.11 Mbp - 20.72 Mbp), chromosome 8 (24.43 Mbp - 26.45 Mbp) and chromosome 9 (19.35 Mbp - 23.24 Mbp) are unknown. The genome is allotetraploid, each haplotype of the assembly contains chromosomes from both sub-genomes.",
